15:48.690 --> 15:51.750
I know.
Now stick your finger in there and twist it.

15:55.396 --> 15:59.857
Hey, Lois. Can I talk to you for a second?
I think we may have a problem with Meg.

16:00.203 --> 16:02.968
You're telling me?
She's been locked in her room all day.

16:03.074 --> 16:05.236
Who knows what she's doing up there?

16:15.385 --> 16:19.847
Yeah, well, the thing is, Meg is becoming
a little enamored with me

16:19.958 --> 16:22.825
and I'm kind of
losing control of the situation.

16:22.929 --> 16:25.626
She's just grateful
you took her to the dance.

16:25.733 --> 16:28.997
Well, I think it's more than that.

16:29.102 --> 16:33.403
So here's the thing, and don't get mad,
and that part I can't stress enough...

16:33.507 --> 16:35.634
That's a great shirt, by the way.

16:35.743 --> 16:38.769
I may have made out with Meg.

16:40.814 --> 16:41.942
Okay, I had that coming.

16:42.049 --> 16:45.110
What the hell is wrong with you?
You sick bastard.

16:45.220 --> 16:47.689
- Look, I was drinking...
- What a shock.

16:49.058 --> 16:52.891
Look, the short version is this morning
she made me eat her hair pie...

16:52.994 --> 16:55.463
No, it's not what you think.
Stewie had some, too.

16:55.564 --> 16:56.555
Stop punching me.

16:56.667 --> 16:59.760
Look, Brian, I don't know
what the hell happened between you two

16:59.870 --> 17:03.533
but you better go upstairs
and straighten it out right now.

17:04.208 --> 17:07.178
This is even worse than when you ate
that bubble-gum out of the garbage.

17:07.778 --> 17:10.441
Brian, did you get
into the garbage last night?

17:11.217 --> 17:13.741
- No. Why?
- Don't lie to me, Brian.

17:13.853 --> 17:15.080
I'm not lying.

17:19.926 --> 17:21.861
Meg, you got a minute?

17:25.699 --> 17:27.429
What the hell?

17:27.536 --> 17:30.061
- I made that for you, Brian.
- Meg!

17:30.172 --> 17:33.573
Look, you obviously didn't
hear me yesterday. So I'll explain it again.

17:33.675 --> 17:34.699
And here to assist me is

17:34.810 --> 17:38.472
Headmaster of the New York School for
the Hard of Hearing, Mr. Garrett Morris.

17:38.579 --> 17:44.383
- Meg, we're not boyfriend and girlfriend.
- We're not boyfriend and girlfriend!

17:44.487 --> 17:50.392
- I will never be attracted to you.
- I will never be attracted to you!

17:50.493 --> 17:56.161
- You're acting like a psycho bitch.
- You're acting like a psycho bitch!

17:56.267 --> 17:58.427
Goodnight and have a pleasant tomorrow.

17:58.535 --> 18:02.304
Goodnight and have a pleasant tomorrow!

18:04.778 --> 18:09.875
- I won't be ignored, Brian.
- I like your ass.

18:23.565 --> 18:24.532
Joe, I gotta tell you.

18:24.633 --> 18:27.033
This whole cop thing ain't as exciting
as I thought it was gonna be.

18:27.136 --> 18:29.002
When do we get to shoot some bad guys?

18:29.105 --> 18:30.969
Guys, it's not all about action.

18:31.073 --> 18:33.405
It's about staying vigilant
until you're needed.

18:33.509 --> 18:36.137
- What are you doing?
- I'm watching Bonnie undress.

18:36.245 --> 18:38.340
- Bonnie's your wife.
- I know.

18:38.449 --> 18:41.417
I like to watch her strip and pretend
she's a woman who I've never met

18:41.518 --> 18:44.579
but who looks just like Bonnie
and lives in my house.

18:44.688 --> 18:46.679
Get naked, you strange whore!

18:46.790 --> 18:49.988
Peter, I haven't seen Meg or Brian
since last night.

18:50.095 --> 18:51.757
I think something may have happened.

18:51.864 --> 18:55.961
Mom, is it bad if I saw Meg
tie up Brian last night,

18:56.067 --> 18:58.629
put him in the trunk of his car
and then drive away?

18:58.737 --> 19:01.265
What? Chris, why didn't you say anything?

19:01.376 --> 19:03.104
I dropped the ball, I'm sorry.

19:03.210 --> 19:07.613
I have just been buried in paperwork
for the past 72 hours.

19:07.714 --> 19:11.617
Oh, my God. Brian was right.
Meg really must be obsessed with him.

19:11.719 --> 19:12.981
Peter, we gotta find them.

19:13.087 --> 19:14.612
Don't worry, Lois, we're the police

19:14.723 --> 19:17.589
and we'll do our very best
to find Brian and girl-Chris.

19:20.663 --> 19:23.633
I'm really having
a great time tonight, Brian.

19:23.733 --> 19:25.997
I can't believe you went to all this trouble.

19:26.102 --> 19:31.096
- Well, you know me.
- I do, Brian. I know you so well.

19:31.208 --> 19:34.007
- So, are you ready?
- For what?

19:34.111 --> 19:38.481
For the fun we're gonna have, Brian.
We're gonna have fun tonight.

19:38.584 --> 19:44.023
Good old-fashioned, all-American fun.

19:44.123 --> 19:48.422
Listen, Meg, I'm not gonna lie to you, here.
I'm a little uncomfortable.

19:48.527 --> 19:51.929
Just relax.
We're gonna be here for a while.

19:52.032 --> 19:55.194
- Well, I don't know if... Wait, what?
- We're gonna be here for a while.

19:55.301 --> 19:57.464
- A while?
- Yeah, a while.

19:57.572 --> 19:59.128
- You mean a while?
- A while.

19:59.239 --> 20:00.537
- A while.
- A while.

20:00.641 --> 20:01.903
- A while.
- A while.

20:02.009 --> 20:03.978
- A while.
- Brian, you're acting weird.

20:04.080 --> 20:06.639
Come on,
that one doesn't even have an "H" in it.

20:06.749 --> 20:10.116
- Don't move, dirtbag.
- Holy crap, what the hell is this?

20:10.219 --> 20:12.120
Brian, she's a teenager.

20:12.222 --> 20:15.281
Yeah, Brian, you're doing the same thing
that Mia Farrow did to that Chinaman

20:15.391 --> 20:17.360
that Woody Allen brought home
from the circus.

20:17.461 --> 20:19.952
Peter, hold on to that thought,
because I'm going to explain to you

20:20.063 --> 20:22.555
when we get home all the things
that are wrong with that statement.

20:22.667 --> 20:25.261
But, first, Meg, you need to let Brian go.

20:25.370 --> 20:29.170
- But Mom, I love him!
- Honey, you're just confused.

20:29.274 --> 20:30.674
I'm not confused.

20:30.776 --> 20:33.678
I've never been more certain
about anything in my life.

20:33.780 --> 20:34.906
I need him.

20:35.015 --> 20:37.883
Meg, I know that's what you think
right now, but you're...

20:37.983 --> 20:40.453
God, I wish I could make you understand.

20:40.554 --> 20:42.247
You don't know what you need.

20:42.355 --> 20:44.789
- I know what she needs.
- You do?

20:44.891 --> 20:48.657
You bet. Bring her by my house
around 8:30 tonight, I'll take care of her.

20:51.133 --> 20:53.762
Hi, Mr. Quagmire.
Mom said I should come over here?

20:53.870 --> 20:57.270
Have a seat, Meg.
Soon, it'll all become clear.

21:02.244 --> 21:05.008
Excuse me,
while I get a little more comfortable.

21:06.081 --> 21:08.812
Meg, I've watched you grow up
from a playful little girl

21:08.918 --> 21:10.978
into a very special young woman.

21:11.089 --> 21:14.616
Now, you probably just think of me as
"square old Mr. Quagmire from next door,"

21:14.726 --> 21:17.752
but, I've been around the block
a few times, learned a couple things.

21:17.863 --> 21:21.354
And I can tell you this,
there's no reason to grow up too fast.

21:21.466 --> 21:23.935
Teenage girls are exposed
to so much these days

21:24.036 --> 21:26.401
I can see why a relationship
looks glamorous.

21:26.505 --> 21:28.063
But, you've got all the time in the world,

21:28.174 --> 21:31.110
and a lot of wonderful experiences
ahead of you.

21:31.212 --> 21:33.702
Hang on, I wanna give you something.

21:34.280 --> 21:36.581
This book helped me
when I was about your age.

21:38.786 --> 21:41.117
It let me know
that as long as I kept on rolling,

21:41.221 --> 21:43.917
I'd find that one person
who would make me whole.

21:44.026 --> 21:47.086
- Thanks, Mr. Quagmire.
- You don't have to thank me.

21:47.196 --> 21:49.721
Now, get on out of here, you little scamp.

21:53.035 --> 21:55.004
All right, ladies, you ready for action?

21:55.105 --> 21:57.903
We sure are, Glenn. Do you have the whip?

21:58.175 --> 21:59.937
Got it right... Wait, what?

22:02.645 --> 22:04.580
Hello, I'm Tom Tucker. Coming up at 11:00,

22:04.682 --> 22:07.676
Quahog police return to active duty
after giving up the search

22:07.785 --> 22:10.880
<i>for fictitious Romancing the Stone
character, Elaine Wilder.</i>

22:10.989 --> 22:13.857
Plus, in national news,
America's Scoutmasters are asking,

22:13.960 --> 22:16.018
"Why are the kids so shy in the shower?"

22:16.129 --> 22:19.030
And, in entertainment,
is Annette Bening made of leather?

22:19.132 --> 22:21.362
A local tanner has a surprising revelation.

22:21.468 --> 22:23.026
We'll have all this, and what else, Ollie?

22:23.137 --> 22:25.400
Sports!
- And sports. Join us at 11:00.

22:25.401 --> 23:26.401
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru